# B3a implementation report

## Changed symbols

- `RejectedCandidateEvidenceV5` is a frozen, pre-materialization rejection carrier with exact type, identity, closed-validation, and round-event-reference shape checks. Its fixed properties expose `experiment_id`, `status == "invalid"`, and exactly one rejection event artifact reference.
- `CandidateRecordEvidenceV5` explicitly unions normal and rejected carriers.
- `ExperimentRecordFactoryV5.build_records`, `_Runtime._expected_records`, and `CanonicalExperimentRecordFactoryV5.build_records` now use that union and optional paired critic inputs.
- The independent expected and concrete constructors both classify exact carrier types, require critic evidence for testable normal candidates, allow no critic only for nonempty no-testable batches, and construct invalid rejected records without materialization or downstream evidence.

## Static reasoning

Rejected-only construction uses an empty internal review mapping and no critic object. Mixed construction derives review IDs only from testable `CandidateEvidenceV5` entries in input order; rejected entries get no review or critic reference. The normal materialized branch retains mandatory critic bindings for every testable status. Rejected records bind the carrier identity, assignment, template, parent semantic authority, fixed invalid validation, and only the durable-event reference; `ExperimentRecordV5` remains the schema/invariant authority. The carrier can validate only the canonical `events/<campaign>/<round>/<sequence>.json` reference shape. B3b must authenticate journal membership and related authority before any persistence.

The runtime call path, publication, recovery, renderer activation, and serialized record schema were not changed. No candidate was materialized, evaluated, persisted, or sent to a model/API during this work.

