## Concerns

The new rejection/record branches are statically reviewed only: no existing authenticated rejection event was available or fabricated, so no end-to-end execution was performed. Persistence and durable event authentication intentionally remain for B3b.

## Fix round 1

Adjusted only `RejectedCandidateEvidenceV5`'s round-event path shape check. The round directory now accepts a digit component of at least four characters and the sequence filename accepts at least six digits before `.json`, matching the repository's minimum-width formatting for values beyond `9999`/`999999`. Event membership and positivity remain deferred to B3b.

Allowed static verification actually run:

- `python -B -m ruff check core/pit_optimizer_v5/runtime.py`; passed.
- In-memory `compile(...)` of `core/pit_optimizer_v5/runtime.py`; completed successfully without bytecode output.
- `git diff --check -- core/pit_optimizer_v5/runtime.py`; completed with only the existing LF-to-CRLF warning.
